'' 'constructor( )' inside a constructor body delegates; it does not open a definition.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/ctor-delegate.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered

'' The delegating constructor calls the default one...
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void _ZN1QC1Ev

'' The namespace closes: before this, 'end constructor' was eaten by the runaway
'' 'constructor( )' and the namespace ran to end of file.
'' EXPECT-NOT: expected 'end NAMESPACE'
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0405

'' ...and the GOLDEN is what pins the ABSENCE of a prologue in the delegating body.
'' A substring assertion cannot say "no second memset"; the whole IR can. Built and RUN
'' against fbc as well: both print '8  107', and a prologue here would print '3' --
'' the fields zeroed after the constructor it delegates to had filled them.
'' GOLDEN: expected/ctor-delegate.out
